#4300
A Cell in the Brig~
   A cell cut into the rock beneath Blackwake's fort and floored with old
ship's planking, black with damp.  A heavy door of iron-bound oak shuts
it off to the east, with a little barred window you can just see through.
There is a bucket in the corner and a heap of mouldy straw, and the
planks of the floor are warped and uneven; in one corner they sit a
little higher than the rest.  Somewhere beneath you, water slaps and
gurgles.
~
