plank planks board boards floor corner~
The floor is made of old ship's planks, warped by the damp.  In the corner
one of them rocks when you press on it, and cold air breathes up around
its edges.  It isn't nailed down.  It might open.
~
E
straw bucket~
Mouldy straw, a bucket you'd rather not look in, and the scratched tally
of some earlier prisoner: thirty-one days.
~
E
window bars door~
Through the little barred window you can see a stone corridor lit by a
lantern, and the boots of someone sitting in a chair.  The boots aren't
moving.  Snoring comes from above them.
~
