#4301
Beneath the Brig~
   You have squeezed down into a crawlspace beneath the brig, between the
planking and the bare rock.  It is barely high enough to crawl, and the
rock is slick with weed; the tide comes in this far, and the water is
ankle deep and cold.  The loose plank is above you, and a passage worn by
the sea leads east, toward the sound of surf.
~
